          "is ever handed.",
          "",
          "Four things English makes you carry,",
          "Indonesian simply has not got.",
          "",
          "   No 'the' and no 'a'.",
          "   No gender on any noun.",
          "   No plural ending.",
          "   No verb endings, and no tenses.",
          "",
          "What it has instead is a handful of",
          "prefixes. The next pages start you off."
        ]
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 4,
        "content": [
          "You already read the alphabet Indonesian",
          "is written in, and nearly every letter",
          "says what you expect. Five do not.",
          "",
          "c is always the ch of chair           Press 1",
          "   cari, to look for; coba, to try",
          "",
          "j is always the j of jam              Press 2",
          "   jadi, to become; juga, too, as well",
          "",
          "ng is one sound, as in singer         Press 3",
          "   dengan, with; orang, a person",
          "",
          "ny is one sound, as in canyon         Press 4",
          "   banyak, many; punya, to have",
          "",
          "And y is always the y of yes, never a",
          "vowel: saya, ya, ayah."
